4,Arequipa-La Unión Quechua - qxu (Quechuan) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/qxu/,"Arequipa-La Unión Quechua (qxu) is part of the Quechuan family and Quechuan, Peripheral Quechua, Chinchay, Southern Chinchay, Southern Peruvian Quechua class.","Quechua, Arequipa-La Unión",Quechuan
5,"In Peru, the Quechua Language Takes to Hip-Hop, Trap, and ‘Q-Pop",https://www.cntraveler.com/story/in-peru-the-quechua-language-takes-to-hip-hop-trap-and-q-pop,"Quechua people have never been a monolithic group, nor a static culture, but rather one shaped by 500 years of resistance since colonization. This evolution of Quechua music reflects that legacy—and provides a potential new future for the language and upcoming generations of speakers.","Quechua, Arequipa-La Unión",Quechuan
6,Common Voice Scripted Speech 26.0 - Quechua Arequipa-La Unión,https://mozilladatacollective.com/datasets/cmqi9x7yx005dnr07mo68a08v,"Arequipa - La Unión Quechua, identified by the ISO 639-3: qxu, belongs to the Quechua II group.Quechua language is written in the Latin script. All Quechua dialects form words by sequentially adding suffixes to a root and follows a Subject-Object-Verb (SOV) word order.","Quechua, Arequipa-La Unión",Quechuan
